resses chosen as \"the ones that changed in the 1-frame step but not in an 8-frame step\"... too fuzzy.\n\nLet me just do: snapshot \"q0\", play_input 1 frame, snapshot \"q1\", diff increased. See which bytes went +1 exactly. In step_frame(1) it was only 0x001F (+1). Let's confirm with a real frame. If 0x001F is the only +1 and yet it's RNG... hmm.\n\nActually wait. Let me reconsider 0x001E/0x001F. In step_frame(1): 0x001F 30→31 (+1). Then step_frame(1) again: 31→196. If step_frame while paused runs the frame properly, 0x001F is not a +1 counter.\n\nBut what if step_frame(1) only ran a PARTIAL frame or the game logic once, and the \"196\" came from extra frames? Confusing.\n\nLet me use play_input(1) which is real. Do it a few times: q0 -> 1 frame -> q1 -> 1 frame -> q2. Find address that goes +1 each time.\n\nLet's do: snapshot q0; play 1; snapshot q1; play 1; snapshot q2; diff q0->q1 increased (name dq1), then diff q1->q2 increased from dq1 (name dq2). The survivor that's +1 both times is the frame counter.\n\nRNG bytes would change, and if they change by arbitrary amounts, \"increased\" keeps them. Hmm, so both rounds keep RNG and counter. But looking at values, the counter is obvious (+1 each).\n\nLet's do it."}
