atch across a Start-press/Start-press cycle.\n\nAlternative: the game mode byte in Zelda is known to control the \"subscreen\" state. Let's find via differential.\n\nLet me first load canonical, then:\nsnapshot gm_closed\nplay_input Start (a few frames) — press start to open subscreen\nwait ~30 frames\nsnapshot gm_open\ndiff changed name m1.\n\nThen pick candidates and watch.\n\nActually a smarter approach: the game mode byte changes immediately on Start and reverts on Start. Use watch with candidates. But we need candidates first.\n\nLet me do the diff.\n\nPress Start: play_input [{buttons:[\"start\"],frames:4},{buttons:[],frames:40}]. Then screenshot to confirm subscreen open. Then snapshot.\n\nLet's do: load_state canonical, snapshot gm_closed. Note load_state runs 1 frame with no input.\n\nThen play start+wait, screenshot, snapshot gm_open.\n\nLet me first load canonical."}
